 # ECS and simulation state
 
+## Experimental mapped table storage (2026-10-29)
+
+Under the default-off `TIDE_PACKED_TABLES` build switch, a table can retain two
+inverse row maps in ordinary COW pages. Get/cell/gather/scatter, growth, removal
+and table moves keep logical row coordinates and entity locations. Explicit
+column/lane loops use physical coordinates; partition must run serially with no
+outstanding pointers/pieces. Removal preserves logical last-row replacement
+while compacting the physical tail separately. The maps are independently
+retained by snapshots and freed with the table.
+
+Hashing, packing, delta bases and repair-page hashes remain in logical order.
+A derived logical-page cache retains exact source/map pages and refreshes
+changed values, rebuilding on map/count changes. The cache is not copied or
+serialized. Stale-page collection refreshes it before collecting logical pages,
+so hashing can still use the ordinary parallel page machinery. Canonical cache
+updates, like table serialization, require a serial boundary. Raw table restore
+starts unmapped. Disabled builds omit both added pointers and mapping branches.
+
+`test_packed_table.c` covers eight sizes around data/map page boundaries and five
+densities, empty/all/none filters, invalid filter columns, inverse maps, physical
+and logical writes, COW snapshots, changing membership, growth, logical removals,
+moves/entity locations, raw saves, deltas from a mapped base, hashes and repair
+page lists. The two new and sixteen existing table/queue checks pass in isolated
+native/WASI executables compiled with the production table source and header.
+Whole-runtime/compiler validation is recorded in packed-storage-integration.md.
+The compiler trial uses transient packing around narrowly eligible numeric
+systems and restores identity before returning; these runtime tests alone do not
+establish correctness of resident packing for arbitrary generated consumers.
+
