 # Language features, as tidec builds them
 
+## Experimental transient row partitions (2026-10-29)
+
+`TIDE_PACKED_TABLES` is a build-time experiment, off by default. A compiler
+built with it emits private wrappers around eligible match systems and an ABI
+marker requiring the same runtime configuration. The default compiler emits
+its existing C and header. This changes no Tide syntax or ordering contract.
+
+Eligibility recursively checks synchronous helper bodies, plain numeric data,
+row-local writes and explicit read-only singleton arguments. Numeric Math calls
+are accepted; C calls, methods/value receivers, queries, World access, queued
+effects, random rolls, tasks, containers, local data and shared writes are
+excluded, including effects hidden through helpers. The first implementation
+also excludes loops, scene filters, shards and tables with more than one sparse
+presence predicate. Compiler-selected sparse storage qualifies just as explicit
+`[Sparse]` storage does.
+
+When activated, the whole tick uses the existing serial scheduler. Before an
+eligible system, the wrapper partitions its matching tables, executes the
+existing physical-column loops, then copies columns back into logical identity
+order through a private helper using existing table APIs. It restores identity
+before any other system or consumer runs. Queries, C systems, queued events and
+structural changes, views, snapshots, saves, deltas and reload therefore retain
+their ordinary logical traversal. Snapshot-shared data pages detach normally;
+retained selection caches reject replaced presence-page identities. No mapped
+layout is retained at a tick or system boundary.
+
+Generated C exposes experimental diagnostics `tide_packed_rows_mode` (0 off,
+1 guarded, 2 forced), `tide_packed_rows_passes` and `tide_packed_rows_count`;
+these are not Tide APIs and are absent from default builds. A test host changes
+mode only between ticks. `TIDE_PACKED_MODE=force`, `auto` or `off` overrides it.
+The provisional auto guard requires 65,536 rows and a nonzero matching fraction
+no greater than 1/16. Forced mode bypasses that heuristic, but counters record
+only actual nonidentity partitions. `TIDE_PACKED_REPORT` reports changed totals
+at tick completion without retaining a callback across game reload.
+
+The gated `packed_rows` e2e fixture requires real packing over 4,103 rows and
+checks pure helper/Math eligibility, helper-hidden C/spawn rejection, shared
+writes, queued tag changes/events, query and extern order, retained snapshots,
+hashes and raw save/restore equality over twelve ticks. The companion generated
+code assertion pins both eligible and excluded systems. Native checks pass;
+native/WASI real `docs/examples/entities.tide` replay passes 360 ticks with 348
+partitions, 3,576 partitioned rows and 34 destructions, preserving state, raw
+saves, deltas and view payloads. Broader validation and timings are recorded in
+packed-storage-integration.md. Conversion and full identity restoration are
+included in timings; this experiment does not establish resident-layout speed
+or complete its integration into other consumers.
+
